      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Dragon Necropolis [CoV]\n**Who:**\n- Researcher Robin - CoV [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 113\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n**Quest Items:**\n- Attuned Piece of Pure Velium [item=140267]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a dragon construct - CoV [npc=56238]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of Dragon Necropolis (10 Points) [quest=10281]\n**Era:** | !Claws of Veeshan\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Oct 29 11:32:38 2020\nModified: Thu May 1 11:28:40 2025 | | **Claws of Veeshan Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**Prerequisite Quests:** None.\nYou can obtain this quest from Researcher Robin in Dragon Necropolis near the zone in.\nYou say, 'Hail, Researcher Robin'\nResearcher Robin greets you as a fellow professional, 'Hail adventurer! I don't know who you upset to get sent to a terrible place such as this, but I'm sure it's the same person I upset. The name's Robin, and I'm a researcher of all things dangerous and deadly and I've come to this necropolis for a better understanding of the [velium] itself. If you have a moment, I could surely use the assistance of an adventurer such as yourself.'\nYou say, ' I can help look into the velium with you.'\nResearcher Robin looks out towards the necropolis and you can see a wince of worry on their face before they continue to speak, 'There are a lot of strange energies emanating from this place. Can't you feel it?' Something feels off.' Researcher Robin gives you a knowing look before they continue, 'I can feel it too, however these energies are difficult to get any further understanding on unless we delve deeper into the [tombs].\nYou say, ' What is happening with the tombs?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'These Old Bones'.\nResearcher Robin says, 'You may have already noticed the large dracholiches that roam these lands. They hold a small key to start our research. Within their bones, where the marrow would be, the velium can accumulate within and that may be what is animating these long dead dragons. These abominations must be cleared out, kill one and inspect its bones. You don't have to be gentle with it, some will probably fall out if you break a bone open while fighting it. Bring me some of the velium that has been from a dracoliche and we can continue our research.'\n\n---\n\n**Task Window Text:** Researcher Robin is studying the velium and how it is reacting differently from within the Dragon Necropolis. He's not much of a fighter and could use your help getting the research he needs in order to fully understand what has happened to the velium.\n1\\. Kill a dracoliche 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n> **Task Window Text:** Slay a dracoliche abomination wandering the surface of the necropolis.\n(Does any dracoliche count for this?)\nAn Attuned Piece of Pure Velium [item=140267] appears on your cursor when the dracoliche dies.\n2\\. Deliver the velium to Researcher Robin 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n3\\. Bring the velium close to dragon bones for Researcher Robin 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n4\\. Bring the velium close to dragon bones for Researcher Robin 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n5\\. Bring the velium close to dragon bones for Researcher Robin 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n6\\. Give the velium close to dragon bones for Researcher Robin 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n7\\. Find the cavern of ice and bring the velium to the statue within 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\nYou can get to the cave easily if you run OVER the building in the middle of the zone, just climb high enough & levitate.\nLoc: neg 219.61, neg 268.94, neg 271.09. This is in final Southern round room where Restless Vaniki can spawn. Updates in correct loc automatically. Room is undead only, some roamers.\n8\\. Return to Researcher Robin and Hail\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n21 AA points\n2% regular exp lvl 125-->126.\n1,42 merc exp points\n**Submitted by:** Gidono, Veludeus",
