      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Dragon Necropolis [CoV]\n**Who:**\n- Bawjitsia Jaradh - CoV [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 113\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n**Quest Items:**\n- Bawjitsia's Bag of Supplies [item=140271]\n- Chetari Inquisitor's Ear [item=140303]\n- Riyaht's Bag of Weapons [item=140302]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Riyaht Lqahla - CoV [npc=56237]\n- a chetari inquisitor - CoV [npc=56207]\n- a restless paebala - CoV [npc=56216]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of Dragon Necropolis (10 Points) [quest=10281]\n**Era:** | !Claws of Veeshan\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Oct 29 11:53:03 2020\nModified: Tue Aug 6 12:28:28 2024 | | **Claws of Veeshan Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**Prerequisite Quests:** None.\nYou can obtain this quest from Bawjitsia Jaradh in Dragon Necropolis. He can be found at /loc 1217, 213, -26 and is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Bawjitsia Jaradh'\nBawjitsia Jaradh looks distressed, but a bit of him lights up the moment you approach him, 'It may not look it adventurer, but you are the exact person I needed right now. Approaching with your head instead of with your sword, I've ran away from 3 fights today from other adventurers that I needed help with, but they thought I was one of the ones taken by the ice.' Bawjitsia Jaradh lowers his shoulders, easing tension for just a moment. It's clear that what he has to say is causing him some grief. 'I'm terrified of what we found within the tomb, and its what has been causing the [conflict].\nYou say, 'conflict'\nBawjitsia Jaradh says, 'Yes, the ice that has infected Velious is less prevalent here, but I think it was because Zlandicar has tricked my brethren into assisting him with some foul magicks. I believe my brethren are blindly following without asking why, which means that they are complacent to what is happening to with the ice. I came across a colony of Paebala who have been infected with the ice and are still doing Zlandicar's bidding blindly. We can try to convince the living ones, but the infected ones can only be stopped with brute force, it is a start, but would you be willing to [help]?'\nYou say, 'help'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Rats of a Feather'.\nBawjitsia Jaradh looks hopeful, 'Thank you, I think together we can get to the bottom of this.'\n\n---\n\n**Task Window Text:** Bawjitsia Jaradh is aware of what is happening within the tomb and the rest of Velious, specifically that it is not something that should be seen to its end and it is something that is big enough to create a truce between the Chetari and the Paebala in the Dragon Necropolis. They have a plan to make sure everyone is ready for when conflict arises as well as make sure everyone agrees to the truce.\n1\\. Slay restless paebala 0/10 Dragon Necropolis\n> **Task Window Text:** Bawjitsia Jaradh has asked you to destroy some of the Paebala that have been infesting the tunnels underneath.\n2\\. Return to Bawjitsia 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n> **Task Window Text:** Return to Bawjitsia Jaradh for further instructions.\nBawjitsia Jaradh appears even more sanguine as you approach. 'Marvelous! With less of the infected Paebala around, that will put a halt to whatever it is they are doing. While you were away, I was able to make contact with a rebel within the paebala who was sympathetic to our cause. They understand the secrecy that must be kept, they can be found outside the walls of the crematorium. Bring them this bag of supplies they need, it will show that you are speaking with them in good faith, and not to kill them.'\nYou receive Bawjitsia's Bag of Supplies [item=140271].\n3\\. Deliver the bag of supplies to Riyaht Lqahla 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n> **Task Window Text:** Bring the bag of supplies to the rebel within the tomb.\n/loc 110, -2565\n4\\. Slay restless chetari 0/10 Dragon Necropolis\n> **Task Window Text:** Riyaht Lqahla has asked you to destroy some of the Chetari.\nRiyaht Lqahla cautiously observes you approach but lets down his guard when they see the bag in your hands, 'Oh, good to see that Bawjitsia Jaradh came through with his end of the deal.' He checks the contents of the bag, 'And its all here. Great! These supplies are needed for my kin to establish a better foothold in the temple. Too many of our brethren have been taken by the ice and Zlandicar has to be the one to blame, it is his infernal device that he brought here! The chetari that have been taken by the ice still serve the mad fool dragon no matter what. You need to clear out some of them, or we will not have a chance to fight back.'\n5\\. Report back to Riyaht 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n> **Task Window Text:** Report back to Riyaht Lqahla for further instructions.\nYou have been given: Riyaht's Bag of Weapons\nRiyaht Lqahla says, 'Great, that will help keep the infected numbers down and we can start on making sure our foothold in the caves is secured. Thank you, adventurer. As part of the deal with Bawjitsia Jaradh, here is a bag of extra weapons we scavenged from unprepared adventurers. Sorry if you knew them but they should have been more prepared going into the caves. If it helps, I know I didn't kill them. So that has to count for something right?'\n6\\. Deliver the sack of weapons to Bawjitsia 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n> **Task Window Text:** Return to Bawjitsia Jaradh with the bag of weapons.\nBawjitsia Jaradh is relieved to see you, 'Well, color me impressed, even Paebala know when it is time to set our differences aside. I expected nothing in return, and you were able to pull through, thank you. There is one more issue that needs to be taken care of, a fanatic who fancies themself an inquisitor. This inquisitor has been gathering a group of other Chetari to thwart our cause for the sake of helping Zlandicar. They need to be silenced, and as it is commonly said, to kill a snake, you must chop off their head. In this case, I will accept an ear.'\n7\\. Kill the Chetari inquisitor 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\nChetari Inquisitor's Ear [item=140303] appears on your cursor when the inquisitor dies.\nThe chetari inquisitor is situated at the end of a tunnel at /way 461, 737, -172\n8\\. Deliver the ear to Bawjitsia 0/1 Dragon Necropolis\n> **Task Window Text:** Give the ear to Bawjitsia Jaradh for proof of your work.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n425 platinum\nYou gain experience!\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
